{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,220p' docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/stories/05-detach-sources-and-preserve-prior-provenance.md\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/tech-design.md | sed -n '640,714p'\"","aggregated_output":"   640\t### Flow 5: Detach Sources\n   641\t\n   642\tThis flow covers AC-5.1 through AC-5.3. Detach is a soft operation. It removes\n   643\tthe source from future active source lists and current-source resolution, but it\n   644\tdoes not delete provenance or mutate an already hydrated working copy mid-run.\n   645\t\n   646\t```mermaid\n   647\tsequenceDiagram\n   648\t    participant U as User\n   649\t    participant C as Client Source UI\n   650\t    participant R as Fastify Source Route\n   651\t    participant S as SourceManagementService\n   652\t    participant P as PlatformStore\n   653\t    participant X as Convex\n   654\t\n   655\t    U->>C: Detach source\n   656\t    C->>R: DELETE source attachment\n   657\t    R->>S: detachSource\n   658\t    S->>P: softDetachSourceAttachment\n   659\t    P->>X: set detachedAt, detachedByUserId, updatedAt\n   660\t    X-->>P: detached row\n   661\t    P-->>S: detached response\n   662\t    S-->>R: detached true\n   663\t    R-->>C: remove from active list\n   664\t```\n   665\t\n   666\t### Flow 6: Reopen and Degraded State\n   667\t\n   668\tThis flow covers AC-6.1 through AC-6.3. Project shell and process work surface\n   669\treads continue to return section envelopes. One failed source/provenance lookup\n   670\tmust degrade locally rather than hiding healthy source rows.\n   671\t\n   672\t`SourceSectionReader` and `MaterialsSectionReader` should preserve the existing\n   673\tsection envelope pattern. Active lists exclude detached rows; process materials\n   674\tuse the active-source resolver to combine project and process scopes. If an\n   675\tenrichment lookup fails, the reader returns durable source identity with\n   676\t`entryStatus: degraded` or a section-level source error only when the whole\n   677\tsection cannot load.\n   678\t\n   679\t## Active Source Resolution\n   680\t\n   681\tThe active-source resolver is the central design answer for process-scoped\n   682\tshadowing. It affects the process work surface and environment working-set\n   683\tplanning; it does not make every project-scoped source automatically current\n   684\tfor every process. A process sees only source attachments referenced by its\n   685\tcurrent material refs, after active filtering and shadowing are applied.\n   686\t\n   687\t```typescript\n   688\texport function resolveActiveProcessSources(args: {\n   689\t  projectSources: SourceAttachmentSummary[];\n   690\t  processId: string;\n   691\t  currentSourceAttachmentIds: string[];\n   692\t}): ProcessSourceReference[] {\n   693\t  throw new NotImplementedError('resolveActiveProcessSources');\n   694\t}\n   695\t```\n   696\t\n   697\tResolution rules:\n   698\t\n   699\t1. Exclude rows with `detachedAt`.\n   700\t2. Build the base active set from rows whose `sourceAttachmentId` is in\n   701\t   `currentSourceAttachmentIds`.\n   702\t3. Partition active rows into project-scoped rows and rows where `processId`\n   703\t   matches.\n   704\t4. Compute shadow key as `${repositoryFullName}:${targetRef ?? ''}`.\n   705\t5. If an active project-scoped row has a process-scoped sibling with the same\n   706\t   shadow key, include the process-scoped sibling in the candidate set even when\n   707\t   its id is not yet in `currentSourceAttachmentIds`.\n   708\t6. Prefer the matching process-scoped row over the project-scoped row for that\n   709\t   process only.\n   710\t7. Sort visible rows by `updatedAt` descending.\n   711\t8. Preserve degraded metadata independently per row.\n   712\t\n   713\tThis resolver belongs in Fastify/shared server logic, not Convex. Convex stores\n   714\trows; Fastify decides how one process sees its current source material.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
